      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name blends Joseph DiGiorgio’s surname with “vista,” reflecting its early agricultural roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/jovista_california",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Jovista sits on a flat alluvial plain at 397 feet, where sandy loam soils support high‑yield fruit and vegetable crops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
